accessWidener v2 official
# Two classes a mod cannot construct at 26.1.x, because both the constructor and the nested
# supplier interface are private and neither has a public factory or Builder:
#   MenuType        - the Resonance Chamber's menu
#   BlockEntityType - the Resonance Chamber's block entity
# The 26.2 branch needs only the MenuType pair; BlockEntityType's constructor is public there.
# That difference is the ONLY source-level change between this branch and 26.2.
#
# TWO javap traps sit behind these four lines, and each one produced a confidently wrong answer:
#  1. The LOOM jar already has Fabric API's transitive access wideners applied, so it reports
#     members as public that a mod genuinely cannot touch.
#  2. The NeoForm jar under common/build/moddev/artifacts/ has THIS FILE's transformer applied to
#     it by the build. So once an entry exists, that jar reports its target as public and reading
#     it "confirms" the entry is unnecessary. Only a jar built with no access transformer at all
#     says what vanilla actually ships.
